WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
A failed refresh must not replace good data
Captioned replay of commands executed on 13 November 2026.
AI-assisted synthetic exercise; not the owner's unaided performance.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:25.000
1 / Reproduce a partial publication
The teaching copy removes the transaction boundary.
The real repository publisher is not modified.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:41.000
2 / Restore the transaction boundary
Diff excerpt: BEGIN wraps validation and all table copies;
COMMIT publishes the complete version. Full diff is downloadable.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:58.000
3 / Repeat the crash, then recover
After the process exits, DuckDB restores the old committed version.
A successful retry publishes the 7-row candidate.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:06.000
4 / Check the existing regressions
Checks include invalid candidates, mid-copy failures,
pre-commit failures, abrupt exit and legacy-view replacement.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:14.000
What this proves - and what it does not
Inspect the captured transcript, evidence JSON and source.
Replay timing is edited for readability; no human narration.
